## 🚀 Key Capabilities

- **🛡️ 100% Invisible to Screen Sharing**: Hardware-level screen protection (`setContentProtection`) ensures your AI overlay never appears in Zoom, Teams, Google Meet, or Webex screenshares or recordings.
- **🎧 Real-Time System Audio Loopback**: Transcribes interviewer speech directly from internal system audio with ultra-low latency (<200ms) using Deepgram Nova-2 models.
- **🧠 Frontier AI Reasoning**: Context-aware answers powered by OpenAI GPT-4o, Anthropic Claude 3.5 Sonnet, and Google Gemini 1.5 Pro.
- **📄 Resume & Job Description Context**: Pre-load your resume and target JD so responses directly reference your actual accomplishments and stack.
- **🎙️ Flexible Capture Modes**: Use **Auto Mode** (continuous detection) or **Push-to-Talk (PTT)** with customizable hotkeys (`Option`, `Space`, or `Control`).
- **🔗 Production Web-to-Desktop Relay**: Built-in deep linking (`interviewbuddy://auth/callback`) for instant email confirmation and password resets.

---

## 💻 Installation & Setup

### 🍎 macOS Installation

1. Download [`Interview-Buddy.dmg`](https://github.com/ganesh-code/InterviewBuddy-Releases/releases/latest/download/Interview-Buddy.dmg).
2. Open the `.dmg` file and drag **Interview Buddy** into your **Applications** folder.
3. Open **Interview Buddy** from Applications or Spotlight.

<details>
<summary><b>⚠️ macOS Gatekeeper / "App is Damaged" Warning? (Click to expand)</b></summary>
<br/>

Because the app is distributed directly outside the Mac App Store, macOS Gatekeeper may show:  
*"Interview Buddy is damaged and can't be opened"* or *"Cannot be opened because the developer cannot be verified"*.

**To resolve this in 5 seconds:**
1. Open your Mac **Terminal** (`Cmd + Space` → type `Terminal`).
2. Paste this command and press Enter:
   ```bash
   xattr -cr /Applications/Interview\ Buddy.app
